astive Evidence:** True Positive SpecificDisease mentions are individuated by a proper name, eponym, or acronym, so the model handles them. The True Positive DiseaseClass \"mental retardation\" has no etiologic or site specifier and is a broad phenotypic umbrella term, so it stays DiseaseClass. The discrepancies are the only cases where a generic head is narrowed by an etiologic or anatomic specifier and no name is present.\n- **Linguistic Rule (Proposed):** Label a disease noun phrase as **SpecificDisease** if it carries an individuating anchor that fixes one nosological entity in the document. Anchors include a proper name, eponym, or acronym, or a premodifier specifying etiology (organism, gene, cause) or anatomic site, even when the head noun is generic (infection, vasculitis, disease, syndrome). Reserve **DiseaseClass** for unmodified or umbrella-level category terms and symptom or phenotype categories. Course and severity descriptors (\"chronic,\" \"acute,\" \"severe\") do not count as individuating anchors on their own. Treat this as a provisional rule, since the boundary between \"cutaneous vasculitis\" (specific here) and broad category terms depends on annotation convention and should be checked against more documents.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3943, "output_tokens": 9930, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 8771}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}